The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'bigquery-public-data': {'epa_historical_air_quality': ['lead_daily_summary', 'pm10_daily_summary', 'voc_daily_summary', 'so2_daily_summary', 'pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary', 'pm25_frm_daily_summary']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `state_name`: filter to “California”.  
• `state_code`: alternative California filter (`'06'`), useful for cross‑checking.  
• `date_local`: filter to year 2020 and extract the month (`EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local)`).  
• `arithmetic_mean`: daily average concentration that will be averaged again (per month).  
• `parameter_name` / `parameter_code`: not needed for the requested aggregates because each table is already parameter–specific, but helpful for verification queries.  
• `units_of_measure`: optional check that the pollutant’s units are consistent.  

Typical conditions  

1. `state_name = 'California'` (or `state_code = '06'`).  
2. `date_local BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'`  (or `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local)=2020`).  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the final combined result.  

```sql
-- 1. Description:  Show all distinct state names that appear in the PM10 table.
SELECT DISTINCT `state_name`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description:  Peek at PM10 daily data for California in 2020.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND date_local BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description:  Monthly average PM10 levels for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS pm10_avg_µg_m3
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description:  Monthly average PM2.5 (FRM) levels for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS pm25_frm_avg_µg_m3
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_frm_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description:  Monthly average PM2.5 (non‑FRM) levels for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS pm25_nonfrm_avg_µg_m3
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description:  Monthly average volatile organic compounds (VOC) levels for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS voc_avg_ppbC
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.voc_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description:  Monthly average SO2 levels (scaled by 10) for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean) * 10      AS so2_avg_ppb_scaled
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.so2_daily_summary`
WHERE state_name = 'California'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description:  Monthly average Lead levels (scaled by 100) for California, 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
